        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "600a74e6-ded2-5be6-a030-011505289cd5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Robinsons-May, The May Department Stores Company, Federated Department Stores, Macy's, Inc.\n- Places: Simi Valley Town Center, Simi Valley, California\n- Organizations: KWSV-LP\n- Topics: mergers and acquisitions, retail anchors, radio broadcasting\n\nFacts:\n- The May Department Stores Company was founded by David May in 1877.\n- On August 30, 2005, Federated Department Stores acquired The May Department Stores Company in a takeover.\n- In 2005, The May Department Stores Company merged with Federated Department Stores, which is now Macy's, Inc.\n- In 2005, Simi Valley Town Center opened with Macy's and Robinsons-May as anchor stores.\n- Robinsons-May was a subsidiary of The May Department Stores Company.\n- Robinsons-May became part of Federated's takeover of The May Department Stores Company.\n- KWSV-LP, branded as 99.1 The Ranch, is a low-power non-commercial country radio station.\n- KWSV-LP has studios inside the Simi Valley Town Center in Simi Valley, California.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "4efec70a-616d-5202-bea9-be677fe79e90",
        "text": "Page: Robinsons-May. Sentence: It was a subsidiary of The May Department Stores Company, having been acquired with Federated's takeover of The May Department Stores Company on August 30, 2005.\nPage: The May Department Stores Company. Sentence: It was founded by David May in 1877, and merged with Federated Department Stores (now Macy's, Inc.) in 2005.\nPage: Simi Valley Town Center. Sentence: The mall opened in 2005 with Macy's and Robinsons-May as anchor stores.\nPage: KWSV-LP. Sentence: KWSV-LP, branded as 99.1 The Ranch, is a low power non-commercial radio station playing a country format with studios located in Simi Valley, California inside the Simi Valley Town Center.",
